hermes-office local patch — NOT an upstream pull request.

Target: clawmem@0.43.5, applied against the installed npm package root
(/usr/local/lib/node_modules/clawmem), AFTER 036, 040, 041 and 042.

Why: patch 040 gave query expansion its own lane and 041 bounded what happens
when that lane's host is off — but the bounded answer is still
expansionFallback(): lex/vec echo the original query and hyde becomes
"Information about <query>", i.e. NO expansion at all. For a lane pointing at a
laptop GPU box that is the normal case, not the exception.

This patch adds one failover hop. When the primary lane produces a typed
fallback — unreachable, in cooldown, transport error, or prose that fails the
lex:/vec:/hyde: contract — a second, always-on endpoint is tried before the
degradation is accepted. A healthy primary costs nothing extra: the failover
instance is only consulted on the fallback path.

Design points worth keeping:

- Separate instance, separate probe/cooldown state. The failover being down must
  not put the primary into cooldown, and a primary failure must not poison the
  failover's lane.
- Only a REAL expansion from the failover replaces the result. A second failure
  leaves the typed fallback in place, so the caller sees the same value it would
  have seen without the feature.
- Both attempts share one deadline (041's fuse). A primary that burned the
  budget hands the failover an already-expired deadline, and expandQuery returns
  its fallback immediately rather than starting a doomed fetch.
- Cache fingerprint gains the failover MODEL NAME (not its URL). Same-name lanes
  — a GPU box and a CPU box running the same fine-tune — keep one key, so an
  expansion cached from either survives the primary going offline. Different
  names split, which is also right. Two endpoints of the same model must NOT
  produce two cache entries; that would re-pay the 3-6s CPU cost every time.
- queryLaneFuseDeadline() also arms when only the failover is configured.

Measured against the production expandQuery path (real store, real DB), primary
= powered-off host, failover = CPU qmd-query-expansion-1.7B:

  primary only (041)        408ms -> typed fallback, no expansion
  primary down + failover   3154/6026/4835ms -> real lex/vec/hyde
  both down                 ~0.8s -> typed fallback, nothing cached
  failover unset            byte-identical to 041

Env:
  CLAWMEM_QUERY_FALLBACK_URL              e.g. http://127.0.0.1:9089/v1
  CLAWMEM_QUERY_FALLBACK_MODEL            optional
  CLAWMEM_QUERY_FALLBACK_API_KEY          optional, falls back to the primary key
  CLAWMEM_QUERY_FALLBACK_REASONING_EFFORT optional
  CLAWMEM_QUERY_FALLBACK_NO_THINK         optional, falls back to the primary value

Retire together with 040/041 if upstream grows a lane chain of its own.

